<title>PHILIPPINES: French Sulzer gets $75 mln Philippine power deal.</title>
<headline>French Sulzer gets $75 mln Philippine power deal.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine power firm Panay Power Corp has awarded a contract to New Sulzer Diesel France S.A. to build a $75 million, 72-megawatt bunker-fired power plant in Iloilo city in central Philippines.</p>
<p>&quot;We have notified New Sulzer Diesel about three to four weeks ago that we have chosen them as our turn key contractor for this Panay power project,&quot;  Peter Garrucho, First Philippine Holdings Corp managing director said.</p>
<p>FPHC owns 50 percent of Panay Power Corp. Other shareholders include Panay Electric Co with a 30 percent stake and First Private Power Corp with a 20 percent interest.</p>
<p>The power plant is scheduled to be ready for commercial operation by the last quarter of 1998.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 fax 8176267</p>
